rev_06 -- WebAssembly linear-memory gate validator
===================================================

FILES
  validator.wasm   A WebAssembly module (hand-assembled). It exports:
                     - memory  (1 page of linear memory)
                     - validate(len: i32) -> i32
  run.js           A small Node harness that loads validator.wasm, writes the
                   candidate bytes into linear memory at offset 0, calls
                   validate(length), and reports the result.

HOW VALIDATION WORKS (from the module)
  The candidate is written to linear memory starting at offset 0. validate()
  walks it byte by byte on the operand stack, folding each byte through a
  state-driven transform, and compares the result against a target block held
  in a data segment higher in linear memory. It returns 1 to accept, 0 to
  reject. There is no stored passphrase -- only what the passphrase becomes.

RUN
  node run.js '<candidate>'                 # candidate as argv, or:
  printf '%s' '<candidate>' | node run.js

Requires Node (any recent version with WebAssembly support). The module
accepts exactly one input. Recover it.
